Note: Understanding PromQL is essential for creating dashboards and alerts.


apiVersion: monitoring.coreos.com/v1
kind: PrometheusRule
metadata:
  name: prediction-alerts
  namespace: monitoring
  labels:
    release: monitoring
spec:
  groups:
  - name: logapp.rules

    rules:

    - alert: NoFileUploads
      expr: increase(prediction_requests_total[5m]) == 0
      for: 2m

      labels:
        severity: warning

      annotations:
        summary: "No log uploads"
        description: "No log files uploaded during the last 5 minutes."

    - alert: TooManyFailures
      expr: increase(prediction_errors_total[5m]) > 5
      for: 1m

      labels:
        severity: critical

      annotations:
        summary: "Too many prediction failures"

    - alert: PredictionRequestsZero
      expr: prediction_requests_total == 0
      for: 30s
  
      labels:
        severity: warning
  
      annotations:
        summary: "Prediction count is zero"
        description: "No prediction requests have been processed."
        description: "More than 5 prediction failures occurred in the last 5 minutes."


Alert-1 Analysis:
      Prometheus asks:

"Has this counter increased during the last 5 minutes?"

If no increase occurred, the expression becomes true.

Then Prometheus waits another 2 minutes (for: 2m).

If it is still true after those 2 minutes, the alert becomes FIRING.
